# DRAFT — not built, not tested, not in any build (2026-10-11)
#
# What this is: an APKBUILD sketch for the PowerVR SGX540 userspace on the Q:
# the TI DDK 1.17.4948957 "ti443x_linux" blobs, unmodified, plus the open glue
# that replaces TI's closed init tool and libdbm. It is the "route A" (native
# musl + gcompat) PRODUCT packaging; route B (glibc sandbox, first light) is a
# procedure, not a package, and is described at the end. Nothing here has been
# built. It follows the project's aport rules (.claude/rules/aports.md) and the
# structure of pmos/nexusq-glibc-rt/APKBUILD.
#
# Short names follow docs/2026-10-11-gpu-sgx540-groundwork.md: ub =
# gpu-sgx540/userspace-blobs.md, ur = usecases-roadmap.md, cd =
# compositor-display.md, kdp = kernel-driver-port.md.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Assumptions, each with its pointer
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A1  The KM is openpvrsgx 1.17.4948957 built in-tree (=m) in
#     linux-google-steelhead (drafts/linux-google-steelhead.APKBUILD.fragment.draft).
#     KM and UM must be the SAME DDK build with the same build-options mask;
#     a mismatch is refused by SGXInit [groundwork §2, ub §3.7, kdp §4].
# A2  Blob set = TI omap5-sgx-ddk-um-linux, branch 1.17.4948957/mesa/glibc-2.35,
#     commit 84a396a4fb379f10931421e489ac8a199d6a9f2c (2024-10-16), target
#     ti443x_linux [groundwork §3 Primary path "UM", ub §2.1]. Re-fetched on
#     2026-10-11 (sparse fetch of LICENSE + targetfs/ti443x_linux only) and
#     hashed; the per-file sha256 below are that measurement, and their first
#     12 characters equal ub §2.1's table.
# A3  Source of the blobs at build time: Maemo Leste sgx-ddk-um, tag
#     1.17.4948957+leste15 = a9dbdc75233dc0ca5fe2622dfffc44f164843c1f
#     (git ls-remote 2026-10-11). Its ti443x/ files are sha256-identical to
#     TI 84a396a4 [ub §2.2, Verification "Maemo sgx-ddk-um"]; the same archive
#     carries the open dbm/ and pvrsrvinit/ sources, so one pinned source
#     serves both. Why not TI directly: abuild cannot fetch git, and the TI
#     cgit snapshot endpoint returned 503 on 2026-10-11 [ub §8, groundwork §6].
# A4  The Maemo tree contains NO TI licence file (its file list at a9dbdc75,
#     GitHub API 2026-10-11, has no LICENSE/COPYING). The TSPA text therefore
#     ships from our aport as LICENSE.TI-TSPA: a verbatim copy of TI
#     84a396a4:LICENSE (6554 bytes, git blob 925cfe51b67bb65067d8eb96217238ac279bca99,
#     sha256 37507b462edf97b59717d2d144daaac85fbca6080c3602b5128e446e97f9ad47).
#     The TSPA requires redistributions to "reproduce this license"
#     (LICENSE:18-20) [ub §8].
# A5  Unmodified means unmodified: options="!strip", no patchelf, no symbol
#     weakening, no dd string patches, ever [ub §8, groundwork §6]. Every
#     shipped blob is checked against A2's sha256 in package(); a mismatch
#     fails the build. This is also the "without modification" proof the
#     release preflight re-checks on the image.
# A6  Not shipped: TI's libdbm blob (replaced by Maemo's LGPL re-implementation),
#     pvrsrvctl (replaced by pvrsrvinit), libPVRScopeServices (profiling only,
#     needs libstdc++) [groundwork §3 "UM", ub §8 packaging design].
# A7  Install prefix /usr/lib/sgx-ddk with the .so and .so.1 links: the
#     unversioned names are dlopen()ed at runtime (libpvr_dri_support loads
#     libGLESv2_PVR_MESA.so, which loads libglslcompiler.so) [ub §3.1, §4.4
#     item 7]. Private directory, MobiAqua-style [ub §2.3, §6 design notes].
# A8  musl route needs (a) libgcompat.so.0 in the GLOBAL scope before the blobs
#     load, (b) a private ld-linux-armhf.so.3 -> /lib/ld-musl-armhf.so.1 link
#     [ub §4.4 items 1-2]. Two ABI hazards stay open and are measured, not
#     patched: mmap@GLIBC_2.4 (32-bit off_t) in libsrv_um and the strerror_r
#     GNU/XSI clash [ub §4.4 items 4 and 8, groundwork TL;DR 9]. If either
#     bites and cannot be shown cold, route A fails the Phase 2 gate and the
#     product stays on route B or fallback F1 [groundwork §3].
# A9  The microkernel firmware is inside libsrv_init.so (.rodata 0x15b94); there
#     is no .fw file to package or fetch [ub §3.6].
# A10 Mesa: the GBM/EGL front end (gallium "sgx") is a SEPARATE aport,
#     nexusq-sgx-mesa, in its own private prefix; Alpine's Mesa 26.2.4 stays
#     untouched [groundwork §3 "Mesa", ur §5.9]. Sketch at the end.
# A11 Licence of Maemo's pvrsrvinit/pvrsrvinit.c is UNKNOWN: the 29-line file
#     has no header and the repo has no COPYING (a9dbdc75, read 2026-10-11).
#     dbm/dbm.c and dbm_helpers.c say "GNU Lesser General Public License as
#     published by the Free Software Foundation" with no version
#     (dbm.c:6-8). Before adoption: ask upstream for a licence statement, or
#     replace pvrsrvinit with our own equally trivial dlopen("libsrv_init.so.1")
#     + dlsym("SrvInit") program. The SPDX ids below are therefore provisional.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Delivery modes and PUBLIC_RELEASE=1 (Petr decides: groundwork §6, §8 q28)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# M1 "redistribute" (groundwork §6 option 1). sgx-ddk-um-ti443x is built from
#    the pinned archive, installed in personal AND public images, and listed
#    in pmos/ota-packages.list (~1 MB; the ti443x deb is 974 KB [ur §6 Phase 6]).
#    Precedents: Maemo main, pmOS non-free 2021-22, our own
#    device-google-steelhead-nonfree-firmware [ub §8].
# M2 "fetch at install" (groundwork §6 option 2). With PUBLIC_RELEASE=1,
#    docker-build.sh installs sgx-ddk-um-fetch INSTEAD of -ti443x; the public
#    rootfs and the gh-pages repo carry no TI binary. The unit downloads the
#    pinned archive on first network, verifies every file against the sha256
#    list shipped in the package, installs into /var/lib/sgx-ddk, and the
#    persist store keeps it across a flash. Personal builds still install
#    -ti443x directly. Caveat: the download is from Maemo's GitHub; a second
#    origin is needed [groundwork §6 option 2 caveat, ub open question 9].
# M3 "private overlay" (the firmware-google-steelhead pattern,
#    docker-build.sh:334-375). If the archive ever disappears upstream, the
#    untouched files are kept in ./private/sgx-ddk/ti443x/ (gitignored),
#    docker-build.sh stages them into the aport after checking each sha256
#    exactly like _fw_stage checks md5, and a public clone without the
#    overlay builds an EMPTY -ti443x (the build succeeds, the GPU stays off).
#    Not the default: the blobs are not secrets and M1/M2 need no overlay.
#
# Release preflight (scripts/release-preflight-no-secrets.sh, to be extended;
# it checks secrets today, not licences [ur §5.11]). Two checks, debugfs on the
# ext4 image like the existing check_* functions:
#   Key both on the TI file NAMES in ti443x.sha256, not on the directory or a
#   *.so.1.17.4948957 glob: the open libdbm we build installs as
#   libdbm.so.1.17.4948957 too (dbm/Makefile.am install-exec-hook) and lives
#   in the same /usr/lib/sgx-ddk.
#   check_sgx_licence: if any TI blob name is present under /usr/lib/sgx-ddk,
#     /usr/share/licenses/sgx-ddk-um-ti443x/LICENSE.TI-TSPA must exist and hash
#     to A4's sha256 [groundwork §6, ub §8].
#   check_sgx_unmodified: every TI blob name present hashes to its pin
#     (debugfs -R "cat <path>" | sha256sum).
#   In M2 additionally: FAIL if any TI blob name is in a PUBLIC_RELEASE image
#     at all.
# Seen failing first: build an image with the licence file deleted, and one
# with a single byte of libusc changed; both must FAIL [groundwork §4 Phase 6].
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Files this aport would carry (to be created at adoption; contents drafted
# here so the review sees them)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LICENSE.TI-TSPA   verbatim TI 84a396a4:LICENSE (A4). Not reproduced in this
#                   draft on purpose: it must be copied byte for byte, then
#                   checked against A4's sha256.
#
# ti443x.sha256     (measured 2026-10-11 from TI 84a396a4, A2)
#   6bdfe93ac40248dd066f0f6f4d85438042194827b49e6140ab926879c576b9f1  libsrv_um.so.1.17.4948957
#   ac329c21ef7507d4663634385f7ee58358cafc1aecff54d4cb3ba01344b0a2f9  libsrv_init.so.1.17.4948957
#   61cb7a4e7cd91265ea6b0646a1d23c72bd8fa3873984c6a7f4a1acb72d0f23ba  libusc.so.1.17.4948957
#   cf65d40e941580e4490924f0897b0dda3d2d2da34975801a3acca8be8e19b9dc  libglslcompiler.so.1.17.4948957
#   b8bcd405e8e310b2c1894757c850d2dc68b782ee951012f2fe1acca7e414c118  libGLESv2_PVR_MESA.so.1.17.4948957
#   3896bb0154fb9318cf97c6951b21b83806165a923bf2d39509cdd3491f29bc48  libGLESv1_PVR_MESA.so.1.17.4948957
#   1a14a453a4db7cb4266cfb3de54bf476e25d10b5cf45b4d85ab52810889905bb  libpvr_dri_support.so.1.17.4948957
#   ba924676fabd81a7a0b326cd7d68d58dade7ea8404b2e17c22132a09e6d32fd2  libpvr2d.so.1.17.4948957
#   (not shipped, A6, recorded for completeness:)
#   c294a8279484eeee07d450fb05a58d89ea658a421a2ea6dde3b65a9caebd22dc  libdbm.so.1.17.4948957
#   b5c6db168bfdebf3cc8903b5bfe1cbad296f3e5b508a218b1e1c9987b864b9ff  libPVRScopeServices.so.1.17.4948957
#   c2adbdf3aaa13edc9461264f2ce78bb7053ee29f159bd35534ccf6e58e75037d  pvrsrvctl
#
# powervr.ini       -> /etc/powervr.ini. Maemo's Droid 4 setting, the first
#                      candidate for us [ub §2.2, §3.5]:
#                        [default]
#                        DisableHWTQTextureUpload=1
#
# 70-nexusq-sgx.rules -> /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/. Starts services init when the
#                      pvr DRM device appears, instead of pmOS's 6x5 s retry
#                      loop [ub §3.4]. The parent driver name "pvrsrvkm" is TI's
#                      template value (50-pvrsrvctl.rules.template, ub §3.4) and
#                      UNVERIFIED for openpvrsgx's pvr-drv.c: read it with
#                      `udevadm info -a /dev/dri/card1` in Phase 1 and fix the
#                      match before adoption.
#                        ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="drm", KERNEL=="card[0-9]*", \
#                          DRIVERS=="pvrsrvkm", TAG+="systemd", \
#                          ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="nexusq-sgx-init.service"
#
# nexusq-sgx-init.service -> /usr/lib/systemd/system/. Pulled in by udev only,
#                      so it has no [Install] section and needs no preset
#                      (aports rule: enable with a preset, never a symlink; a
#                      udev-wanted unit is not enabled at all). While the KM is
#                      blacklisted (kernel draft §8) the device never appears at
#                      boot and this never runs.
#                        [Unit]
#                        Description=PowerVR SGX540 services init (SrvInit, uploads the microkernel)
#                        Documentation=file:///usr/share/doc/sgx-ddk-um/README
#                        ConditionPathExists=|/usr/lib/sgx-ddk/libsrv_init.so.1
#                        ConditionPathExists=|/var/lib/sgx-ddk/lib/libsrv_init.so.1
#                        [Service]
#                        Type=oneshot
#                        RemainAfterExit=yes
#                        Environment=LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/lib/sgx-ddk:/var/lib/sgx-ddk/lib
#                        ExecStart=/usr/libexec/sgx-ddk/pvrsrvinit
#                        Nice=10
#                        TimeoutStartSec=30
#      Runs as root: pmOS's package said "(WARNING: runs as root)" [ub §3.4].
#      No ExecStop: SrvInit has no counterpart in pvrsrvinit; unloading is
#      `rmmod` with no client open (kdp §12 step 6). UNVERIFIED whether a second
#      SrvInit after a module reload is accepted; Phase 1's 10 load/start/unload
#      cycles answer it [groundwork §4 Phase 1 exit].
#
# nq-sgx-fetch + nq-sgx-fetch.service   (subpackage -fetch, mode M2 only)
#      Oneshot, After=network-online.target, Wants=network-online.target,
#      ConditionPathExists=!/var/lib/sgx-ddk/.complete. busy-box sh script:
#        1. wget the pinned archive (A3) into a mktemp dir under /var/lib/sgx-ddk;
#        2. tar -x ONLY the eight shipped names of ti443x.sha256 from
#           sgx-ddk-um-<sha>/ti443x/usr/lib/ (not the libdbm blob, not Scope, A6);
#        3. sha256sum -c against /usr/share/sgx-ddk-um/ti443x.sha256 (shipped
#           in the package): any mismatch = delete the temp dir, exit 1, no
#           partial install;
#        4. move into /var/lib/sgx-ddk/lib, create the .so/.so.1 links (the
#           ld-linux-armhf.so.3 link comes from -open in /usr/lib/sgx-ddk),
#           touch .complete;
#        5. never modify a file after verification (A5).
#      A failed unit is a loud diag finding and the app shows "GPU userspace
#      not installed" [ub §8 fallback design]. Persist across a flash with a
#      bind mount from /var/lib/nexusq/persist/sgx-ddk, the same pattern as
#      nexusq-persist-roon.mount (ConditionPathIsMountPoint on the store).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

pkgname=sgx-ddk-um
pkgver=1.17.4948957
pkgrel=0
_ti_commit=84a396a4fb379f10931421e489ac8a199d6a9f2c	# TI ti443x blobs (A2)
_maemo_commit=a9dbdc75233dc0ca5fe2622dfffc44f164843c1f	# tag 1.17.4948957+leste15 (A3)
pkgdesc="PowerVR SGX540 userspace (TI DDK 1.17.4948957, ti443x) and its open glue"
url="https://github.com/maemo-leste/sgx-ddk-um"
arch="armv7"
# Provisional, see A11. The main package is empty; the subpackages carry the
# real licences.
license="LicenseRef-TI-TSPA AND LGPL-2.0-or-later"
# !strip: the TSPA allows only UNMODIFIED binaries (A5).
# !tracedeps: the blobs NEED libc.so.6 / ld-linux-armhf.so.3, which no Alpine
#   package provides by that name (same reason as nexusq-glibc-rt).
# !archcheck: glibc armhf ELF on purpose. !check: no host tests for blobs;
#   the seen-failing tests are the preflight checks above and the probe.
options="!strip !check !tracedeps !archcheck"
depends="$pkgname-open"
makedepends="autoconf automake libtool libdrm-dev mesa-dev"
subpackages="
	$pkgname-ti443x:_ti443x
	$pkgname-open:_open
	$pkgname-fetch:_fetch
	"
source="
	sgx-ddk-um-$_maemo_commit.tar.gz::https://github.com/maemo-leste/sgx-ddk-um/archive/$_maemo_commit.tar.gz
	LICENSE.TI-TSPA
	ti443x.sha256
	powervr.ini
	70-nexusq-sgx.rules
	nexusq-sgx-init.service
	nq-sgx-fetch
	nq-sgx-fetch.service
	"
builddir="$srcdir/sgx-ddk-um-$_maemo_commit"

_blobs="libsrv_um libsrv_init libusc libglslcompiler libGLESv2_PVR_MESA
	libGLESv1_PVR_MESA libpvr_dri_support libpvr2d"

prepare() {
	default_prepare
	# Refuse to build from anything but the pinned, unmodified TI files (A5).
	cd "$builddir"/ti443x/usr/lib
	for _b in $_blobs; do
		grep " $_b.so.$pkgver\$" "$srcdir"/ti443x.sha256
	done | sha256sum -c - || die "ti443x blobs differ from TI $_ti_commit"
	# The licence must be TI's text byte for byte (A4).
	echo "37507b462edf97b59717d2d144daaac85fbca6080c3602b5128e446e97f9ad47  $srcdir/LICENSE.TI-TSPA" \
		| sha256sum -c - || die "LICENSE.TI-TSPA is not TI 84a396a4:LICENSE"
}

build() {
	# Open glue only (libdbm, pvrsrvinit), built natively for musl. configure.ac
	# needs pkg-config libdrm and gbm (configure.ac:41-42 at a9dbdc75); Alpine's
	# gbm headers are used for compiling only.
	autoreconf -fi
	./configure \
		--prefix=/usr \
		--libdir=/usr/lib/sgx-ddk \
		--bindir=/usr/libexec/sgx-ddk \
		--sysconfdir=/etc
	make
}

package() {
	# Meta package (depends= above): the open glue, which in turn needs ONE
	# blob provider, -ti443x (M1, personal builds) or -fetch (M2).
	mkdir -p "$pkgdir"
}

_ti443x() {
	pkgdesc="PowerVR SGX540 TI DDK 1.17.4948957 ti443x blobs, unmodified (TI TSPA)"
	license="LicenseRef-TI-TSPA"
	provides="sgx-ddk-um-blobs=$pkgver-r$pkgrel"
	depends="!$pkgname-fetch"
	local _d="$subpkgdir"/usr/lib/sgx-ddk _b
	install -dm755 "$_d"
	for _b in $_blobs; do
		# install -m, never strip/patch: the bytes stay TI's (A5).
		install -m755 "$builddir"/ti443x/usr/lib/$_b.so.$pkgver "$_d"/
		ln -s $_b.so.$pkgver "$_d"/$_b.so.1
		ln -s $_b.so.$pkgver "$_d"/$_b.so
	done
	install -Dm644 "$srcdir"/LICENSE.TI-TSPA \
		"$subpkgdir"/usr/share/licenses/$pkgname-ti443x/LICENSE.TI-TSPA
	install -Dm644 "$srcdir"/ti443x.sha256 \
		"$subpkgdir"/usr/share/$pkgname/ti443x.sha256
}

_open() {
	pkgdesc="PowerVR SGX540 open glue: libdbm (LGPL), pvrsrvinit, init unit, apphints"
	license="LGPL-2.0-or-later"	# provisional, A11
	depends="gcompat libdrm sgx-ddk-um-blobs"
	local _d="$subpkgdir"/usr/lib/sgx-ddk
	make -C "$builddir" DESTDIR="$subpkgdir" install
	# Maemo's install also drops etc/profile.d/mesa.sh
	# (MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE=pvr, Makefile.am:6-7). Not wanted system wide:
	# the TI-aliased Mesa picks omapdrm without it [ub §3.1], and only GPU
	# clients get the private prefix [ur §5.9].
	rm -f "$subpkgdir"/etc/profile.d/mesa.sh
	rmdir "$subpkgdir"/etc/profile.d 2>/dev/null || true
	# glibc loader name -> musl, so a blob's NEEDED ld-linux-armhf.so.3 resolves
	# to musl itself [ub §4.4 item 2]. Not gcompat's PIE loader.
	ln -s /lib/ld-musl-armhf.so.1 "$_d"/ld-linux-armhf.so.3
	install -Dm644 "$srcdir"/powervr.ini "$subpkgdir"/etc/powervr.ini
	install -Dm644 "$srcdir"/70-nexusq-sgx.rules \
		"$subpkgdir"/usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70-nexusq-sgx.rules
	install -Dm644 "$srcdir"/nexusq-sgx-init.service \
		"$subpkgdir"/usr/lib/systemd/system/nexusq-sgx-init.service
}

_fetch() {
	pkgdesc="PowerVR SGX540 TI blobs, fetched and sha256-verified at install (public images)"
	license="MIT"
	provides="sgx-ddk-um-blobs=$pkgver-r$pkgrel"
	depends="!$pkgname-ti443x"
	install -Dm755 "$srcdir"/nq-sgx-fetch "$subpkgdir"/usr/libexec/sgx-ddk/nq-sgx-fetch
	install -Dm644 "$srcdir"/nq-sgx-fetch.service \
		"$subpkgdir"/usr/lib/systemd/system/nq-sgx-fetch.service
	install -Dm644 "$srcdir"/ti443x.sha256 "$subpkgdir"/usr/share/$pkgname/ti443x.sha256
	install -Dm644 "$srcdir"/LICENSE.TI-TSPA \
		"$subpkgdir"/usr/share/licenses/$pkgname-ti443x/LICENSE.TI-TSPA
	# The blobs land in /var/lib/sgx-ddk/lib, filled by the unit. NOT a
	# /usr/lib/sgx-ddk symlink: -open installs libdbm and the loader link into
	# that real directory, and apk must never write through a symlink into
	# state the unit owns. GPU processes search both directories:
	#   LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/lib/sgx-ddk:/var/lib/sgx-ddk/lib
	install -dm755 "$subpkgdir"/var/lib/sgx-ddk
	# The unit needs an [Install] and a preset line (95-nexusq-*.preset style,
	# pmos/device-google-steelhead/nexusq.preset) -- device package side.
}

sha512sums="
SKIP  sgx-ddk-um-$_maemo_commit.tar.gz
SKIP  LICENSE.TI-TSPA
SKIP  ti443x.sha256
SKIP  powervr.ini
SKIP  70-nexusq-sgx.rules
SKIP  nexusq-sgx-init.service
SKIP  nq-sgx-fetch
SKIP  nq-sgx-fetch.service
"
# (sha512sums are regenerated by `pmbootstrap checksum` at adoption, never
# hand-edited; SKIP here only because nothing was downloaded for this draft.
# GitHub archive tarballs are not guaranteed byte-stable over time, which is
# why the per-file sha256 check in prepare() is the real pin, not the tarball
# sha512.)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Open points for the route A product (measured in Phase 2, never patched
# into the blobs) [ub §4.4, §10]
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# - gcompat in the global scope. pvrsrvinit is a musl executable that
#   dlopen()s libsrv_init.so.1 -> libsrv_um.so.1, and libsrv_um imports
#   __printf_chk/__snprintf_chk/__vsnprintf_chk, which only gcompat has
#   [ub §4.3]. Link pvrsrvinit with `-Wl,--no-as-needed -l:libgcompat.so.0`
#   (DT_NEEDED => global, AFTER libc) or start it with LD_PRELOAD (BEFORE libc).
#   The order decides who gets which strerror_r [ub §4.4 item 8]; pick on the
#   strace/gdb evidence, not by guess.
# - strace -f -e trace=mmap,mmap2,openat,ioctl of pvrsrvinit and of the first
#   GLES client: which DRM nodes open, and what offset PVRSRVMapDmaBuf passes
#   [groundwork §4 Phase 2, ub §10 step 3]. No further disassembly of TI blobs
#   (TSPA; groundwork §6 compliance note).
# - Route A is first-of-its-kind for the 2024 blobs on musl [ub §6 A].
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Companion aport sketch: nexusq-sgx-mesa (separate APKBUILD at adoption)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One mesa-sgx in a private prefix, never replacing Alpine's Mesa (no glvnd in
# Alpine; soname collision otherwise) [groundwork §3 "Mesa", ur §5.9]:
#   candidates (build both once, pick one) [groundwork §3, ub §10 step 1]:
#     TI      https://github.com/TexasInstruments/mesa  powervr/24.0.1
#             7c82c1eebc67f5a62a347a84d42fe795cf7f523b (has the 2025-01 render-node fix)
#     mobiaqua https://github.com/mobiaqua/mesa-sgx  mesa-22.3-sgx head a698020
#   meson: -Dllvm=disabled -Dgallium-drivers=sgx,softpipe
#          -Dgallium-sgx-alias=omapdrm -Dgbm=enabled
#          -Dplatforms=wayland (drm/surfaceless come with GBM/EGL) [ub §3.1, §10 step 4]
#   prefix /usr/lib/sgx-mesa: libEGL.so.1, libgbm.so.1, libGLESv2.so.2,
#          dri/omapdrm_dri.so; GPU clients only, via
#          LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/lib/sgx-mesa:/usr/lib/sgx-ddk [ub §6 design notes].
#   depends="sgx-ddk-um". It requires the 2024 blobs: every current SGX Mesa
#   frontend looks up PVRDRIRegisterVersionedCallbacksV0 [ub §3.1].
#   Toolchain risk on Alpine edge (GCC 15, C23) [ub §3.1].
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Route B, glibc sandbox, FIRST LIGHT ONLY (a procedure, not an OTA package)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Purpose: prove KM + blobs + Mesa on our kernel with the fewest unknowns; a
# failure here is KM/DT/clock, not ABI [groundwork §3 row 1, ub §6 B].
#   1. On the HOST, copy the pinned bookworm base (nexusq-glibc-rt tarball,
#      pmos/nexusq-glibc-rt/APKBUILD) to a new tree; never modify
#      /opt/glibc-rt itself (Roon's sandbox).
#   2. Unpack into it, with dpkg-deb -x, from Maemo daedalus
#      (https://maedevu.maemo.org/leste/, Packages index of 2026-10-11) [ub §2.2,
#      groundwork §4 Phase 2]:
#        sgx-ddk-um-ti443x 1.17.4948957+leste15-1+4m7 (Depends libc6 >= 2.34)
#        sgx-ddk-um-tools  (pvrsrvinit; version UNVERIFIED, same source package)
#        libegl-mesa0, libgbm1, libgl1-mesa-dri 22.3.6+sgx2-1+4m7
#        plus their Debian bookworm armhf closure (libllvm15 alone is
#        100,245 kB installed) [ub §6 B, Verification correction 6].
#      Do NOT use excalibur's Mesa 24.0.9-sgx1: it needs glibc >= 2.38, bookworm
#      has 2.36 [ur §5.8].
#   3. Copy the tree to the unit's rootfs (> 100 MB: flash/scp only, NEVER the
#      OTA repo [groundwork §4 Phase 2]).
#   4. Start services init inside it, as root, with the pvr device bound:
#        bwrap --bind <tree> / --dev /dev --dev-bind /dev/dri /dev/dri \
#              --proc /proc --ro-bind /sys /sys --ro-bind /etc/powervr.ini /etc/powervr.ini \
#              /usr/bin/pvrsrvinit
#      (bwrap pattern of roon-nexusq [ub §6 B]; the exact flag set is
#      UNVERIFIED and is settled in Phase 2.) Then eglinfo/es2_info, kmscube
#      on the CURRENT mode, under timeout + nice, frame-capped
#      [groundwork §4 Phase 2-3, §7].
#   5. Nothing from route B ships. The product is route A (this APKBUILD) or
#      fallback F1, decided at the Phase 2 gate [groundwork §3, §4 Phase 2].
